{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>To meet Elohim.</b> To meet the heavenly host that passes before the Holy One, blessed be He, as it says immediately after: וַיֵּרֶד ה׳ עַל הַר סִינַי (Exodus 19:20)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "Sforno quotes the Aramaic phrase דְּחָלְפֵי קַמֵּיהּ דְּקוּדְשָׁא בְּרִיךְ הוּא ('that passes before the Holy One, blessed be He'); the English rendering follows the Aramaic idiom directly. Verse citation normalized."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:18.686192405Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}